{
  "id": "queue-kanji-turn-order",
  "title": "A deck and the deckless source in one tier: the rebuild after an answer continues with the other source's unit, it does not restart at the deck (C-28c)",
  "covers": [
    "queue.kanji_turn_order"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "new_per_day is 4. The deck 'Words' (priority 0) holds the new kana words うっかり (card ...10) then Ｔシャツ (card ...20). The deckless source (scheduler.mined_priority default 0: the same tier) holds the new word 学校 (card ...30), created before its kanji notes 学 (card ...40) and 校 (card ...50), both new and deckless.",
    "Step 0: both sources have no new card today; the deck goes first on the tie: うっかり. Then the deckless source (0 < 1): the unit [学, 校, 学校], 4 of 4. Ｔシャツ does not fit. Order: うっかり, 学, 校, 学校. until_stop is 4.",
    "Step 1 answers うっかり Easy. Step 2: the deck has one new card today, the deckless source none, so the deckless unit is drawn first and fits (3 of 3): 学, 校, 学校, the tail of step 0 (QueueBuilder rule 4 'Turn order'). A round-robin restarted at the deck would draw Ｔシャツ, and the unit would lead with 学, 校 and lose its word. until_stop is 3.",
    "Step 3 answers 学 Easy. Step 4: 学 is the last new card and the deckless source's next word requires it (open unit): 校, 学校. until_stop is 2. The deckless kanji cards do not count as turns of the deckless source."
  ],
